                        "form_id": "5424353b-078a-45f7-823c-4366b65534c4",
                        "entry_id": "9ef6b9fc-69e2-3884-83e2-22e965c4e2c6",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more mephitic"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "2ceb7551-1792-4aa8-98c8-a55324db009c",
                        "entry_id": "9ef6b9fc-69e2-3884-83e2-22e965c4e2c6",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most mephitic"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "184a27c3-4237-3dc2-a418-1e9c0f61e36b",
                        "entry_id": "9ef6b9fc-69e2-3884-83e2-22e965c4e2c6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Foul-smelling or noxious, particularly of a gas or atmosphere."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "61a0dfdf-b636-4df4-9513-45db82b80f19",
                                "sense_id": "184a27c3-4237-3dc2-a418-1e9c0f61e36b",
                                "text": "\"I could have borne the sight of his crutch,\" said she, \"but the crutch and the nephew together really oppress me like a mephitic vapour.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5dd7ac76-0414-460d-9c38-76e1c6648afe",
                                "sense_id": "184a27c3-4237-3dc2-a418-1e9c0f61e36b",
                                "text": "It is impossible to convey, in words, any idea of the hideous phantasmagoria of shifting limbs and faces which moved through the evil-smelling twilight of this terrible prison-house. Callot might have drawn it, Dante might have suggested it, but a minute attempt to describe its horrors would but disgust. There are depths in humanity which one cannot explore, as there are mephitic caverns into which one dare not penetrate."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0c1b00e4-9676-413a-927d-53ac0707f584",
                                "sense_id": "184a27c3-4237-3dc2-a418-1e9c0f61e36b",
                                "text": "From this crawling flapping mass of obscene reptilian life came the shocking clamor which filled the air and the mephitic, horrible, musty odor which turned us sick."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6c751409-fdf5-45c3-a8a5-cc7d4d601c5c",
                                "sense_id": "184a27c3-4237-3dc2-a418-1e9c0f61e36b",
                                "text": "More than that, perhaps the worst thing, was a sort of mephitic fog, moistureless and invisible, that came and went like an exhalation of the arid earth itself."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
